<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8" />
  <title>VIP Multi-Horizon Screen — {{ symbol }}</title>
  <style>
    body { font-family: Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif; margin: 2rem auto; max-width: 960px; color: #222; line-height: 1.45; }
    h1, h2 { font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; }
    table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 1rem 0 1.5rem; font-size: 0.92rem; }
    th, td { border: 1px solid #ccc; padding: 0.4rem 0.55rem; text-align: left; }
    th { background: #f3f3f3; }
    .meta { color: #555; margin-bottom: 1.5rem; }
    .caveat { margin: 0.4rem 0; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <h1>Volatility Intelligence Platform — Multi-Horizon Factor Screen</h1>
  <p class="meta">
    Symbol: <strong>{{ symbol }}</strong><br />
    Study: {{ study_id }}<br />
    Generated: {{ generated_on }}<br />
    Horizons: {{ horizons_label }}
  </p>

  <h2>Research question</h2>
  <p>
    Which models predict next-day, next-week, and next-month close-to-close
    realized volatility under walk-forward evaluation with primary metric
    <code>qlike</code> (lower is better)?
  </p>

  <h2>Locked methodology (per horizon)</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Inference baseline: <code>{{ baseline_model }}</code></li>
    <li>Significance level α={{ alpha }}</li>
    <li>
      “Significantly better” only when the primary block bootstrap rejects at α
      <em>and</em> mean ΔQLIKE &lt; 0; otherwise use descriptive QLIKE wording.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>horizon_days</th>
        <th>target</th>
        <th>embargo</th>
        <th>nw_lags</th>
        <th>bootstrap_block_length</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      {% for row in per_horizon_rows %}
      <tr>
        <td>{{ row.horizon_days }}</td>
        <td><code>{{ row.target_column }}</code></td>
        <td>{{ row.embargo_size }}</td>
        <td>{{ row.nw_lags }}</td>
        <td>{{ row.bootstrap_block_length }}</td>
      </tr>
      {% endfor %}
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Skill by horizon</h2>
  <p class="meta">
    Cross-horizon mean OOS QLIKE and bootstrap inference vs HAR.
    Rankings alone are descriptive, not findings.
  </p>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>horizon_days</th>
        <th>model</th>
        <th>qlike</th>
        <th>mse</th>
        <th>mae</th>
        <th>mean ΔQLIKE</th>
        <th>bootstrap CI</th>
        <th>bootstrap p</th>
        <th>significant_vs_baseline</th>
        <th>vs HAR</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      {% for row in horizon_rows %}
      <tr>
        <td>{{ row.horizon_days }}</td>
        <td>{{ row.model }}</td>
        <td>{{ "%.6f"|format(row.qlike) }}</td>
        <td>{{ "%.6f"|format(row.mse) }}</td>
        <td>{{ "%.6f"|format(row.mae) }}</td>
        <td>
          {% if row.mean_delta_qlike is not none %}
            {{ "%.6f"|format(row.mean_delta_qlike) }}
          {% else %}—{% endif %}
        </td>
        <td>
          {% if row.bootstrap_ci_low is not none and row.bootstrap_ci_high is not none %}
            [{{ "%.6f"|format(row.bootstrap_ci_low) }},
             {{ "%.6f"|format(row.bootstrap_ci_high) }}]
          {% else %}—{% endif %}
        </td>
        <td>
          {% if row.bootstrap_pvalue is not none %}
            {{ "%.4f"|format(row.bootstrap_pvalue) }}
          {% else %}—{% endif %}
        </td>
        <td>
          {% if row.significant_vs_baseline is not none %}
            {{ row.significant_vs_baseline }}
          {% else %}—{% endif %}
        </td>
        <td>{{ row.comparison_note }}</td>
      </tr>
      {% endfor %}
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Caveats</h2>
  <ul>
    {% for caveat in caveats %}
    <li class="caveat">{{ caveat }}</li>
    {% endfor %}
  </ul>
</body>
</html>